# Canonical shared denylist.
# NOTE: `.known-bad.locklist.local` is gitignored and never committed. It's a
# machine-local place to add your own denylist entries without touching this
# shared file (e.g. to react to a fresh incident before it's reviewed and
# merged here). It is loaded in addition to this file and does not need to
# match it — a fresh clone of this repo will not have a .local file at all.
# ===========================================================================

# Supported entry formats (one per line):
#   - package@version
#   - package@*                 (block any version)
#   - package                   (block any version)
#   - package@version#sha512-... (block exact artifact)
#
# Parsing rules:
#   - blank lines reset comment context
#   - comments are ignored by the scanner
#   - nearby WHY/REF/TAGS/POLICY comments may be shown in --explain output
#
# Review metadata:
#   - update LAST-REVIEWED whenever you review or materially change this file
#   - REVIEW-NOTE is optional and meant for quick human context
#
# LAST-REVIEWED: 2026-09-29
# REVIEW-NOTE: Re-audited live dependency tree after the Sep 29 ncu bump; no active matches.
# Added the Sep 23, 2026 MemTensor/sckit worm and May 2026 node-ipc entries. Completed the
# keyv/cacheable block from CSA advisory AD-2026-009 (@cacheable/node-cache, @cacheable/net,
# ecto). Checked the Jun 2026 IronWorm incident (asteroiddao web3 packages, e.g. weavedb-*);
# not present and unrelated to this stack, so not listed.


