# --- Keyv / Cacheable ecosystem compromise (Aug 4, 2026) ---
# WHY: Maintainer GitHub account compromised; malicious preinstall hook (Shai-Hulud-lineage
# worm) stole credentials and self-propagated. Reaches this repo transitively via
# eslint -> file-entry-cache -> flat-cache -> keyv (dev dependency chain).
# TAGS: supply-chain, worm, maintainer-compromise, preinstall
# REF: incident-2026-keyv-cacheable
